## Caddy edge for the local-public dashboard demo
##
## T7.1 of plan 2026-05-29-dashboard-public-integration-canonicalization.
##
## Topology (droplet 165.227.121.20 OR any host with public DNS pointing at it):
##
##   browser → Cloudflare DNS (A record) → droplet :80/:443
##                                          → Caddy (this file)
##                                            → localhost:5173  (vite dev server)
##                                            → localhost:13002 (loopzero-cloud via port-forward)
##                                            → localhost:14433 (ory-kratos-public via port-forward)
##
## Auto-HTTPS via Let's Encrypt HTTP-01 challenge on :80.
## Certs persist under /var/lib/caddy by default (or $XDG_DATA_HOME).
##
## Start with: `task cloud:caddy:up` (binds :80/:443, requires sudo).
## Stop with:  `task cloud:caddy:down`.
##
## Required prereqs:
##   - Caddy >= 2.7 installed
##   - Cloudflare DNS A records pointing app/cloud/auth.loopzero.example at the host
##   - `task cloud:port-forward:up` to expose loopzero-cloud + ory-kratos locally

{
  email admin@loopzero.example
}

# Dashboard (vite dev server with HMR) + same-origin Kratos proxy
# Per 2026-06-01 security-first mandate: Kratos session endpoints (/sessions/*,
# /self-service/*) reverse-proxied via app.loopzero.example so XHR from the dashboard
# is SAME-ORIGIN — eliminates SameSite=Lax cross-subdomain cookie ambiguity
# entirely. Cookies travel unconditionally on same-origin XHR.
#
# Host header REWRITTEN to auth.loopzero.example so Kratos sees its expected host
# (matching serve.public.base_url and CORS allowed_origins). Flow.ui.action
# still emits auth.loopzero.example absolute URLs — those are submitted via top-level
# form POST (which carries Lax cookies on cross-origin top-level navigation
# without issue), and the OIDC callbacks land on auth.loopzero.example (matching
# GitHub/Google OAuth Client redirect_uri registration).
app.loopzero.example {
  # WebSocket route MUST come first to win the match priority
  @ws {
    header Connection *Upgrade*
    header Upgrade websocket
  }
  reverse_proxy @ws localhost:5173

  # Kratos session endpoints — same-origin proxy
  handle /sessions/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14433 {
      header_up Host auth.loopzero.example
    }
  }
  handle /self-service/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14433 {
      header_up Host auth.loopzero.example
    }
  }

  # Dashboard SPA (everything else → vite)
  reverse_proxy localhost:5173
  encode gzip
}

# Cloud auth/billing service
cloud.loopzero.example {
  reverse_proxy localhost:13002
  encode gzip
  # Stripe webhook posts here; Caddy needs to pass through raw body for signature
  # validation (cloud's billing webhook handler reads request body before parsing
  # — Stripe-Signature HMAC depends on the exact bytes received).
  request_body {
    max_size 1MB
  }
}

# Kratos public (browser-facing login/registration flows)
auth.loopzero.example {
  reverse_proxy localhost:14433
  encode gzip
}

# ============================================================================
# DEV-PUBLIC env (plan 2026-06-04-dev-public-domain-canonicalization, T1.1)
# ============================================================================
# Mirrors the auth/app/cloud blocks above on *-dev.loopzero.example so dev test
# infra can coexist with the legacy *.loopzero.example (reserved for prod cutover).
# Cookie domain = loopzero.example — shared by both env so dashboard cross-host
# session works identically. OAuth callbacks for the dev OAuth apps go to
# https://auth-dev.loopzero.example/self-service/methods/oidc/callback/{provider}.

app-dev.loopzero.example {
  # Plan release-blockers-2026-06-25-set T1.1 + T2.1 (closes #44+#45+#46+#47).
  # Canonical 5-header response set mirrors dashboard/nginx.conf prod posture
  # + HSTS (the 5th the Red Team flagged missing). Applied at every response
  # from this host block (proxied or served). Closes #44 clickjacking + #45
  # nosniff/Referrer/HSTS gap on the SPA.
  header {
    X-Frame-Options "DENY"
    X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
    Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
    Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://auth-dev.loopzero.example https://cloud-dev.loopzero.example; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://auth-dev.loopzero.example https://accounts.google.com https://github.com; frame-ancestors 'none'"
    Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
  }

  # T2.1: gate Vite dev paths to 404 — closes #46 (source TS + HMR client leak).
  # These paths only exist in `vite dev` mode (npm run build doesn't emit them).
  # Local dev workflow uses localhost:5173 directly (not via Caddy), so this
  # only blocks the PUBLIC host.
  handle /src/* {
    respond 404
  }
  handle /@vite/* {
    respond 404
  }
  handle /node_modules/.vite/* {
    respond 404
  }

  @ws {
    header Connection *Upgrade*
    header Upgrade websocket
  }
  reverse_proxy @ws localhost:5173

  handle /sessions/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14433 {
      header_up Host auth-dev.loopzero.example
    }
  }
  handle /self-service/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14433 {
      header_up Host auth-dev.loopzero.example
    }
  }

  # Plan J-09 T1.1 (2026-06-05) — GitHub App install handshake.
  # The dashboard's "Install GitHub App" button uses a RELATIVE URL
  # (/v1/integrations/github/install?return_to=...). Without this
  # handle the request hits Vite and 404s, breaking the install flow.
  # Proxy /v1/integrations/github/* to loopzero-cloud so install + callback
  # both work from app-dev.loopzero.example. Cookies are set with Domain=
  # loopzero.example (AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN) so they travel cross-subdomain
  # back to cloud-dev when GitHub redirects.
  handle /v1/integrations/github/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:13002 {
      header_up Host cloud-dev.loopzero.example
    }
  }

  # T6.2 follow-up canonical (2026-06-12 sponsor walkthrough catch): loopzero-cloud
  # API endpoints (/v1/auth/me, /v1/auth/session/token, /v1/projects, /v1/billing,
  # etc) accessed cross-origin from dashboard would require CORS, but loopzero-cloud
  # has CORS disabled per MEET-040 (same-origin assumption). Mirror the existing
  # /sessions/* + /self-service/* + /v1/integrations/github/* same-origin pattern
  # for ALL /v1/* paths so dashboard fetches against relative URLs travel cookies
  # canonical + CORS not needed. Aligns dev-public arch with MEET-040 via edge.
  handle /v1/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:13002 {
      header_up Host cloud-dev.loopzero.example
    }
  }

  reverse_proxy localhost:5173
  encode gzip
}

cloud-dev.loopzero.example {
  # Plan release-blockers-2026-06-25-set T1.2 (closes #47).
  # HSTS at the edge — the Go cloud middleware already emits CSP/nosniff/XFO/
  # Referrer; only HSTS was missing per Red Team #47.
  header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"

  # Plan J-09 T4.1 (2026-06-06) — GitHub webhook bypass cloud auth proxy.
  # GitHub does NOT send JWT/cookie -- it signs the body with HMAC-SHA256
  # using the App's webhook secret. loopzero-api validates that signature
  # directly (api/internal/github/webhook/handler.go). Routing this path
  # through the loopzero-cloud /engine proxy would require adding a public
  # (no-JWT) route there, widening loopzero-cloud's attack surface for no
  # benefit. Instead Caddy hands the request straight to loopzero-api:3001
  # so the HMAC check is the single boundary -- defense in layers via
  # TLS at edge + HMAC at app. loopzero-cloud stays JWT-only.
  handle /api/v1/webhooks/github {
    reverse_proxy localhost:13001 {
      header_up Host loopzero-api.loopzero-system.svc.cluster.local
    }
  }

  # Canonical surface is app-dev.loopzero.example as of 2026-06-22 per
  # qa-dogfood-cleanup-2026-06-21 #128/#122 (QA walkthrough audit).
  # Everything OTHER than the GitHub webhook redirects to the canonical
  # host so external CLI consumers + doc bookmarks don't 404 silently.
  # 301 permanent so browsers + the LoopZero CLI follow + update bookmarks.
  handle {
    redir https://app-dev.loopzero.example{uri} 301
  }
}

auth-dev.loopzero.example {
  # Plan release-blockers-2026-06-25-set T1.3 (closes #45 — HSTS on /auth-dev).
  # Kratos/Hydra public endpoints assert HSTS at the edge.
  header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"

  # Plan J-05 (2026-06-05) — Hydra public routes. The device-flow
  # verification_uri Hydra emits is https://auth-dev.loopzero.example/oauth2/device/verify,
  # so browser must reach Hydra (port-forward localhost:14444), not Kratos.
  # Same for the OIDC discovery document, JWKs, userinfo, and credentials
  # endpoints that OIDC clients hit on auth-dev directly. handle blocks
  # are first-match-wins, so the default Kratos proxy below catches the rest.
  handle /oauth2/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14444
  }
  handle /.well-known/* {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14444
  }
  handle /userinfo {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14444
  }
  handle /credentials {
    reverse_proxy localhost:14444
  }
  handle /admin/* {
    # Hydra admin should NEVER be exposed publicly; deny defense-in-depth.
    respond "Not Found" 404
  }
  # Default: Kratos public (self-service flows, sessions, health, ui).
  reverse_proxy localhost:14433
  encode gzip
}

# J-23 preview-dev wildcard — Vercel-like PR previews
#
# ONE Caddy block + ONE Cloudflare wildcard A record cover EVERY future
# PR for every tenant + project automatically. Zero per-PR config.
#
# URL convention: <internal-sni>.preview-dev.loopzero.example
#   where <internal-sni> is the IngressRoute Host match the manifest
#   builder emits via appHostname(), e.g.,
#   "tn-08fa2ecedc3c7e77-teste-api-preview-pr-1".
#
# The {http.request.host.labels.3} expression extracts the first label
# from the public hostname (Caddy indexes labels RIGHT-to-LEFT, so for
# `foo.preview-dev.loopzero.example` → labels.3 = "foo"). The Host header
# forwarded to the workload Traefik LB substitutes the .loopzero.local
# suffix, matching the IngressRoute exactly.
#
# Cloudflare DNS: wildcard A record `*.preview-dev.loopzero.example` →
# 165.227.121.20 (proxied=false; preserves HTTP-01 challenge path).
#
# TLS — DNS-01 via Cloudflare (J-23 #68 of 4-task batch, 2026-06-07):
# Per-host HTTP-01 against a wildcard hits LE's "50 certs/week per
# Registered Domain" rate limit within a single dogfood session. Wildcard
# cert via DNS-01 needs the `caddy-dns/cloudflare` plugin baked into the
# binary (stock Caddy ships without DNS providers). Build path codified
# in `infra/scripts/local/caddy-build-with-cloudflare.sh` — produces
# `/usr/local/bin/caddy` with the cloudflare TXT-record updater wired.
#
# The CF API token MUST have Zone:DNS:Edit on loopzero.example (operator
# provisions via `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=…` env var — canonical name shared
# with `taskfiles/infra.yml` dev-public:dns precondition + the 5 scripts
# under `infra/scripts/{local,production,drill}/`). `task dev-public:caddy`
# reads it from the running process env. NEVER inline the token in this
# file — the Caddyfile is checked into git.
#
# Pre-condition: a Caddy build that includes caddy-dns/cloudflare. Run
#   bash infra/scripts/local/caddy-build-with-cloudflare.sh
# once per host; idempotent. `caddy list-modules | grep dns.providers`
# must show `dns.providers.cloudflare` for this block to issue certs.
*.preview-dev.loopzero.example {
  tls {
    dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
    resolvers 1.1.1.1
  }
  reverse_proxy https://172.18.0.10:443 {
    header_up Host {http.request.host.labels.3}.loopzero.local
    transport http {
      tls_insecure_skip_verify
    }
  }
  encode gzip
}

# J-25 prod-dev wildcard — production deploy URLs (Vercel-canonical)
# URL convention: <project>-<env>.prod-dev.loopzero.example
# Per ADR D1 of plan 2026-06-12-dashboard-journey-j25-live-url-discoverability,
# loopzero-api status.go:252 emits this format when BASE_DOMAIN=prod-dev.loopzero.example
# (configured in infra/helm/loopzero-api/values-dev.yaml — Tilt-canonical for
# dev-public per memory `feedback_tilt_owned_deployment_yaml_drift`).
#
# Pattern parallel to *.preview-dev.loopzero.example (J-23 delivered 2026-06-07):
# Caddy rewrites external `<project>-<env>.prod-dev.loopzero.example` →
# internal `<project>-<env>.loopzero.local` so Traefik IngressRoute matches.
# labels.3 extracts the 3rd dot-separated label from the request host:
#   `foo-production.prod-dev.loopzero.example` → labels.3 = "foo-production"
#   `kitchensink-production.prod-dev.loopzero.example` → labels.3 = "kitchensink-production"
#
# Cloudflare DNS prerequisite: wildcard A record `*.prod-dev.loopzero.example`
# → droplet IP (parallel to existing `*.preview-dev.loopzero.example` record).
# Without this DNS step, the Caddy block is unreachable from the public
# internet — operator MUST add the CF DNS record before sponsor walkthrough.
#
# TLS via Cloudflare DNS-01 challenge (LE prod). CF_API_TOKEN env var
# canonical (same as preview block above).
*.prod-dev.loopzero.example {
  tls {
    dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
    resolvers 1.1.1.1
  }
  reverse_proxy https://172.18.0.10:443 {
    header_up Host {http.request.host.labels.3}.loopzero.local
    transport http {
      tls_insecure_skip_verify
    }
  }
  encode gzip
}
